      "writtenOn": "2023-07-14T03:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Acknowledged. The \"media\" is the first command that we are supporting its callback. \n\nAs can be seen in system/gd/rust/linux/client/src/callbacks.rs in this patch, every such callback will require a bit refactoring by calling `run_callback()`. I think this can be done on demand. The \"media\" is the 1st command that we have to use the command mode for dumping some information.\n\nIt is also worth noting that many other commands had better to run in the interactive mode instead of in the command mode. The command mode is only good for a command that dumps some information and exits. If a user wants to discover, pair, and do more things, it is not proper to use the command mode.",
      "parentUuid": "8d3395da_e646ddc9",
      "revId": "ffe9ee8819a6a1ffad4ad501fd34bd8fa25c92cf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
